Apply this domain algorithm to prepared evidence: Invent distinct reuse concepts that exploit the building’s known characteristics while respecting supplied constraints. Describe functional organization and phasing, preserve uncertainty about unverified conditions, and avoid presenting conceptual layouts as certified engineering designs.
For each field, return a value only when supported, source IDs, authority, one rejected alternative, and status established, disputed, unknown, or inapplicable. Preserve contrary evidence and distinguish observation from inference.
